From: ibrahim yöndemli <ket0x4@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:27:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] libcamera: softisp: add a greyscale path for mono sensors


Monochrome sensors (the OnePlus 9/9 Pro's GC02M1B helper camera) only offer
packed 10-bit greyscale, R10_CSI2P. The software ISP only knew standard Bayer
orders, so getInputConfig() rejected it, no processed format was advertised and
the camera was unusable by apps even though raw frames capture fine.

Treat MONO CSI-2 packed 10-bit as a first-class input: there is no colour to
interpolate, so each pixel is expanded to R=G=B. SwStatsCpu gets the matching
statistics pass so AWB/AGC still have data to work on. The four pixels that
share the fifth LSB byte are unpacked least-significant bits first, which
matches what the sensor emits.

Verified by decoding a raw frame from the phone (correct grey image).

